      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For example: I want a subtitle to pop up when I get to a certain frame of an animation.I add the the string \"newSubtitleIndex\" and the int \"4\" to a SetProgramVariable call from the event.\nUsing an on value change event for \"newSubtitleIndex\" inside the UdonBehaviour, I pass on the new index to my subtitle manager and then trigger its playing of the subtitle using that data.\nNote that we can pass an Object in, too. This means we could pass in another UdonBehaviour, or be able to pass in a string held inside a TMP text field, etc.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-16T12:21:00.777Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "(Also, whitelist it as a valid Animation Event!)\nAllowing us to pass an AnimationEvent into a UB's SetProgramVariable would allow us to then use the on value change feature that was recently added to drive code actions. This would allow us to use animation events more flexibly.\nSee: https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/script-AnimationWindowEvent.html",
